---
description: Enforce safe live-update behavior with channel discipline, compatibility gating, and rollback readiness
alwaysApply: true
---

live-update-guardrails:

- Treat live updates as web-layer OTA only; native changes still require store release.
- Always ensure app startup calls `CapacitorUpdater.notifyAppReady()` after critical initialization.
- Use staged rollout progression (for example: `staging -> beta -> production`).
- Before promotion, run compatibility checks against target channel metadata.
- Determine release type before OTA shipment; if release type is native, stop OTA flow.
- Capture current channel bundle before changing any channel assignment.
- Require rollback target bundle to be identified before production rollout.
- For risky updates, define explicit blast-radius limits (channel filters and platform targeting).
- Avoid immediate forced reload during sensitive flows without a user-safe fallback.
- Validate post-rollout telemetry: startup success, update failures, crash deltas.
- For metadata-sensitive changes, set minimum update version strategy explicitly.
